e-personnel-security walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the termination checklist + access-revocation runbook + travel
briefing, authored and self-reviewed in-session against the NIST SP 800-53
Rev. 5 Personnel Security (PS) family (csrc landing fetched 2026-10-10) and
CISA Insider Threat Mitigation (cisa.gov, fetched 2026-10-10, 62,166 bytes).

Scope: fictional Copperline Freight; voluntary resignation of a sysadmin with
domain-admin rights, two weeks' notice. Checklist (what/owner/when): day-0 HR
system date + risk-rating + access inventory; days 1-10 knowledge transfer;
day 10 shared-credential rotation (admin passwords, service accounts, PSKs,
safe combos); last-day exit interview + asset return + NDA reminder; COB
revocation (disable, not delete — preservation per e-investigations); day+1
verification (login attempt fails, rotation confirmed); day+30 privileged
post-departure review. Involuntary variant: revocation before the meeting,
escort, asset collection at the meeting. Travel briefing: CFO high-risk trip —
loaner device, minimal data, no customer DB over hotel net, border-inspection
assumptions, documented acknowledgment, scheduled debrief with device
inspection + credential rotation.

